<%# ICODOS override of app/views/submit_form/_docuseal_logo.html.erb %>
<%#
  Header on the document signing page, the surface external counterparties see.
  The "Powered by DocuSeal" line is required here: LICENSE_ADDITIONAL_TERMS asks
  for attribution in interactive user interfaces, and this is one.

  Sized with inline styles on purpose. This view is compiled into the `form`
  CSS pack, whose Tailwind content set is narrower than the application pack's,
  and the overlay files are never scanned at image build time either way. The
  classes used here (mx-auto, flex, flex-col, items-center) are all present in
  the form pack; anything new must be checked before it is used:
    grep -F 'the-class' /app/public/packs/css/form-*.css

  width/height are the file's intrinsic pixels, so the browser reserves the box
  before the image arrives and the signing header does not jump.
%>
<a href="<%= root_path %>" class="mx-auto flex flex-col items-center">
  <img src="/icodos-logo.png" alt="ICODOS" width="732" height="255" decoding="async" style="height: 2.2rem; width: auto; object-fit: contain;">
  <span style="font-size: 0.65rem; color: #7e7e7e; margin-top: 0.3rem; letter-spacing: 0.03em;">Powered by DocuSeal</span>
</a>
